<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91573" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῡρᾰμοῦς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦντος</span>, ὁ, 
			contr.
		 fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυραμόεις, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cake of roasted wheat and honey</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ephipp.
				8.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Trypho
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.114b
			</span></i>; given to him who kept awake best during a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παννυχίς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				2.6P.
			</span></i>: hence, generally, <i>meed of victory, prize</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ γὰρ τεχνάζειν ἡμέτερος ὁ π.</span> for
			stratagem 'we take the <i>cake</i> (or <i>biscuit</i>)', <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				94
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eq.</u>
				277
			</span></i>.</div>
